WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.680
The cast of American Pickers is known for
finding treasures inside mountains of garbage.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.529
And just like the Pickers themselves, we've
scrounged through the lives of Mike Wolfe,

00:00:11.529 --> 00:00:15.709
Frank Fritz, and Danielle Colby, as well as
some of their more notable guests. Sit back

00:00:15.709 --> 00:00:19.420
and enjoy some behind-the-scenes facts from
American Pickers. You won’t even have to

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.030
get your hands dirty.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.270
They have humble beginnings

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.510
The art of finding a valuable item in a pile
of junk isn't something that can be learned

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:31.090
overnight. It takes years of practice to hone
those trashy skills, and Mike Wolfe definitely

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:35.719
has plenty of practice. His passion for junk
started during his childhood, after he sold

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:40.629
a bike he found for $5. From there, he began
lurking in alleyways and derelict houses hoping

00:00:40.629 --> 00:00:44.739
to find anything worth a couple of bucks.
He also made a habit of harassing farmers

00:00:44.739 --> 00:00:49.159
until they let him look through their barns
for old bicycles, which he bought for $50

00:00:49.159 --> 00:00:52.370
and sold for up to $5,000. Quite the racket.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:56.809
Frank, on the other hand, was a building inspector
before he signed on with longtime friend Mike.

00:00:56.809 --> 00:01:01.589
So, while his interest was casual, it hit
hard once the show started to film.

00:01:01.589 --> 00:01:02.679
Mike is an author

00:01:02.679 --> 00:01:07.270
There's always the danger that some more curious
vocations will become a lost art. Well, Mike

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:11.590
Wolfe has already taken action to make sure
that doesn't happen to picking. First, Wolfe

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:16.210
penned Kid Pickers: How to Turn Junk into
Treasure, a children's tome on how to do what

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:20.700
he does. He also started a website with the
same name, providing little pickers with a

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.619
social media outlet and community to keep
them all connected. Looks like Wolfe's got

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:26.969
a little junk army forming.

00:01:26.969 --> 00:01:28.549
Mike doesn’t want to be a star

00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:33.140
Despite all the fame Wolfe and company have
gained since American Pickers captured American

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:37.119
hearts, he doesn't think they deserve it.
According to Wolfe, the real stars are the

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:41.969
eclectic characters, like Hippie Tom, Hobo
Jack, and Prince Mongo, who allow the pickers

00:01:41.969 --> 00:01:45.869
to root through their belongings in search
of gold. Wolfe goes on to say that viewers

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:49.689
remember the people, not what was bought from
them. Wolfe remarked in an interview with

00:01:49.689 --> 00:01:53.950
Entrepreneur.com, "it's always been an honor
that people open their homes and their hearts

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.200
to us." Quite the honor.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.740
Mike doesn’t seem to have too many skeletons
in his closet. Well, except for this one:

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.800
"Hahahahaha!"

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.319
Frank, on the other hand...

00:02:04.319 --> 00:02:06.380
Frank Fritz was taken to court

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:10.420
One of the criticisms of American Pickers
is that they basically rip people off by buying

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:15.950
things cheap so they can sell them for a huge
profit. It other words, capitalism. It didn't

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:20.640
help when Frank Fritz was sued for allegedly
swindling a South Carolina man named Jerry

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.720
Bruce. The collector needed a polarimeter
for a museum he wanted to open, he offered

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.890
to buy one from the Pickers, since he saw
them purchase one on their show. Fritz offered

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:33.550
to sell it to him for $300, but after Bruce
sent his check, he never got his purchase,

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:37.920
nor was the check cashed. Bruce took Fritz
to court, and Fritz wound up losing the case

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.560
by simply not showing up. Ultimately, Bruce
was awarded $1000 for an investment of zero

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.180
dollars, which is a deal even the Pickers
would be envious of.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.950
Danielle wears more than one hat

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:53.180
Ever the entrepreneur, American Pickers’
Danielle Colby doesn't limit herself to picking

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:57.150
through junk. Before she gained fame on the
History Channel hit series, she earned a living

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:01.700
by working as a burlesque dancer, which she
continues to do. But she doesn't just dance.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.090
Her devotion to this art form is such that
she's also produced a documentary focusing

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:11.970
on Tempest Storm, a legendary dancer with
a career that spans decades. For a time, Danielle

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:16.560
also owned a little boutique of her own, 4
Miles 2 Memphis, which was located not far

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.600
from American Pickers headquarters, and is
also a former roller derby competitor.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.010
Danielle may also be a tax dodger

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:28.410
Perhaps because she has her hands in so many
vocations, Colby's had a habit of forgetting

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:33.650
to give Uncle Sam his cut of the action. Back
in 2013, the IRS informed Colby that she owed

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:38.760
just under $6,000 in unpaid taxes from her
boutique. And that was just her first notice.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:43.560
Over the next couple of years, she received
at least four more warnings. By 2015, she

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.690
reportedly hadn't paid any of the money she
owed, which continued to snowball, even though

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:53.090
she clearly understands business. Let's hope
her other business ventures are squared away.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:54.810
Hobo Jack is an author too

00:03:54.810 --> 00:04:00.360
World renowned hobo and American Pickers regular
"Hobo Jack" Sophir isn't any ordinary hobo.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:05.280
He's published three books, including the
classic Amazing Adventures of the Tramp Prince.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:10.190
In addition to his literary ambitions, Backwoods
Jack, as he's also known, fancies himself

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:15.020
a musician. Playing guitar and piano by ear,
Jack has released five albums. According to

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:19.320
his website, since he handles the orders himself,
it could take "weeks or months" for orders

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.100
to be fulfilled. Get your copies now!

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.380
Prince Mongo has political aspirations

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:30.560
Though he only appeared on the show once,
Robert "Prince Mongo" Hodges is quite unforgettable,

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.560
as the residents of his hometown know all
too well:

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.540
"I've come to Earth, to save the Earthlings."

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:41.130
When we met the Memphis resident, he dwelled
within a crumbling castle that he called Ashlar

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:47.200
Hall. As the King of Zambodia, he gave away
his castle in 2014 to businessman Kenny Medlin.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:51.510
The only problem was that he’d kinda already
given it to someone else first, resulting

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:57.920
in a complicated legal situation. He's also
run for mayor numerous times since 1991:

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:02.340
"May the good spirits be with you! All the
way!"

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.020
People have tried to cash in on "Mole Man"
Ron's fame

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:10.200
"Mole Man" Ron appeared in one episode of
American Pickers' first season, during which

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:14.540
the guys crawled through his insane burrow
hoping to find some goodies. The purple-hooded

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.639
Marty Feldman lookalike gained enough fame
that someone else attempted to cash in on

00:05:18.639 --> 00:05:24.200
it. In June of 2011, an ad was posted on Yard
Sales Pittsburgh promoting a sale featuring

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:28.990
items from the Mole Man's burrow. Mole Man
himself wasn't listed as an attendee, but

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:33.710
the ad did mention he'd be stopping by from
time to time. It's very possible that almost

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:36.670
everyone who went to this sale "just missed
him."

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:40.980
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:45.970
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which dark secrets you think the American

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:46.470
Pickers are hiding...

